steps.body:
To count the rooms a day of meetings needs, sort the meetings by start. Then keep a `MinPriorityQueue` of end times, one per room, so `ends.front()` is the room that frees up first.

For each meeting, if the earliest end is at or before its start, that room is free: dequeue it. Then enqueue the meeting's own end:

```javascript
const { MinPriorityQueue } = require("@datastructures-js/priority-queue");
const meetings = [[10, 12], [9, 11], [11, 13], [14, 15]];
meetings.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]);
const ends = new MinPriorityQueue();
for (const [start, end] of meetings) {
  if (!ends.isEmpty() && ends.front() <= start) {
    ends.dequeue(); // that meeting is over: reuse its room
  }
  ends.enqueue(end);
}
console.log(ends.size()); // 2
```

The `<=` is the rule for meetings that touch: a meeting that ends at 11 frees its room for one that starts at 11. Write `<` instead when a room stays booked through the minute its meeting ends. Check `isEmpty()` first, because `front()` on an empty heap is `null`, and `null <= 9` is `true`.

Each meeting enqueues one end and dequeues at most one, so the heap never shrinks, and its size at the end is the answer. It only grows when even the earliest end is after the start, and then every meeting inside is still running. Sorting costs O(n log n) and each heap step O(log n), so the whole count is O(n log n), with O(n) extra space.

example.code:
const { MinPriorityQueue } = require("@datastructures-js/priority-queue");
const input = require("fs").readFileSync(0, "utf8");

const interviews = input.trim().split("\n").map((line) => {
  const [name, start, end] = line.trim().split(/\s+/);
  return [name, Number(start), Number(end)];
});
interviews.sort((a, b) => a[1] - b[1] || a[2] - b[2]);

const ends = new MinPriorityQueue();
for (const [name, start, end] of interviews) {
  if (!ends.isEmpty() && ends.front() <= start) {
    ends.dequeue();
    console.log(`${name}: reuses a room`);
  } else {
    console.log(`${name}: new room`);
  }
  ends.enqueue(end);
}
console.log(`Rooms: ${ends.size()}`);

